  "verbalization": "Lupinifolin appears to have a shared target, C8166, across multiple cell lines, suggesting a potential role in modulating the activity of C8166. The evidence indicates that Lupinifolin interacts with SK-MEL-28 and T47D, which are both targets of different compounds—2-(5-Hydroxy-1H-Indol-3-Yl)Acetic Acid and Ixerisoside A, respectively. These compounds are likely involved in signaling pathways that influence the function of C8166. The integration of these pathways suggests that Lupinifolin may act through a common mechanism, possibly by modulating the activity of these target compounds, thereby influencing C8166. The evidence supports a relationship where Lupinifolin's effects are mediated through these intermediaries, highlighting a potential regulatory role in the biological processes of C8166.",
